nal second arm: small 1-hidden MLP (hidden 32, GELU) to test capacity effect (A).\n3. **Periodic de-normalization (PD)**: forecast = backbone_output\u00b7\u03c3 + \u03bc_seq(target phases), per-phase means of the future H_out steps rolled from the cycle bank.\n- **(A)** Input H=48 (2 periods); output H_out \u2208 {6, 12, 24}, primary H_out=24. **(A)** P=24 (period given as hyperparameter, matching CycleNet) with an ACF/FFT estimator on the training set used as a **diagnostic only** (period is not learned in the core model).\n\n## 4 Training setup (all planned)\n- Loss: **MSE** (primary); **MAE** reported alongside.\n- Optimizer: **Adam** LR 1e-3 (A); control optimizer SGD+momentum (optional, A). LR schedule: ReduceLROnPlateau or cosine (A).\n- Early stopping on val MSE (patience 10); max 100 epochs (A); batch 64 (A).\n- Per-channel zero-mean/unit-variance scaling applied outside the periodic transform.\n- Seeds {0,1,2} fixed; metrics reported as mean\u00b1std over seeds.\n\n## 5 Baselines, controls & comparison structure (transparent ablation)\nAll arms share identical split, windows, seeds, and preprocessing \u2014 only the periodic transform is toggled on/off, so the marginal effect of the CycleNet periodic component is isolated.\n\n| # | Arm | Description | Role |\n|---|-----|-------------|------|\n| B1 | **Lag-P naive (seasonal persistence)** | \u0177(t+h)=x(t+h\u2212P) | Reference for skill score; model-free upper bound of difficulty for periodic series |\n| B2 | **Phase-mean** | \u0177(t+h)=\u03bc[phase(t+h)] (from cycle bank) | Weakest periodic baseline; checks whether learned values add anything over the pure template |\n| C1 | **Backbone only (no PN/PD)** | same architecture, raw scaled input | Core ablation: effect of the periodic component |\n| M1 | **CycleNet (backbone + PN + PD)** | full planned model | Main arm |\n\nControl discipline: B1\u2013M1 evaluated on identical (windowed) test set; M1 vs C1 differs ONLY by periodic transform; same seed init for C1/M1; deterministic data generation seed.\n\n### Planned comparison grid (model \u00d7 metric \u00d7 horizon)\n| Horizon | Metrics | B1 lag-P | B2 phase-mean | C1 backbone-no-PN | M1 CycleNet |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| H_out=6 | MSE, MAE, SS vs B1 | compute | compute | compute | compute |\n| H_out=12 | MSE, MAE, SS vs B1 | compute | compute | compute | compute |\n| H_out=24 | MSE, MAE, SS vs B1 | compute | compute | compute | compute |\n\nWhere **skill score SS = 1 \u2212 MSE_model/MSE_B1** (positive \u21d2 beats seasonal persistence). SS is computed per horizon. Reported as mean\u00b1std over 3 seeds per cell.\n\n## 6 Analysis plan (all planned)\n- **Primary metrics**: MSE, MAE, SS vs B1 per horizon (grid above).\n- **Diagnostics**: \n  - (a) ACF/FFT estimated period vs true P=24 (period recovery);\n  - (b) period-sensitivity: run M1/C1 with P\u00b11, \u00b12 (A) \u2014 expected (planned hypothesis, not a result) PN degrades more gracefully than no-PN;\n  - (c) noise-level sweep \u03c3_noise (A);\n  - (d) backbone capacity: linear vs small MLP;\n  - (e) ACF of PN residual at lag P \u2248 0 (periodic structure removed before backbone).\n  - (f) per-phase error profile (error mapped to phase-of-period to locate where residuals concentrate).\n- **Sanity checks**:\n  - (S1) On a pure-noise control series, M1 must NOT beat B1 (guards against leakage/overfitting artifacts).\n  - (S2) Round-trip unit test on noiseless pure sine: PN \u2192 (identity backbone) \u2192 PD \u2248 original.\n  - (S3) Convergence check: train loss decreases, val loss plateaus (early stopping).\n  - (S4) Seed reproducibility: low cross-seed variance.\n  - (S5) Leakage audit: cycle-bank stats computed only from history up to each origin; test windows never intersect train/val.\n\n## 7 Feasibility (planned)\n- Implementable with stdlib only: matrix ops via lists/math, batched sliding windows in pure Python, SGD/Adam math by hand. (Verified stdlib available; deps absent \u21d2 this is the req